                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "OK, understand I am 64 years young. Been around since before stuff like this was a thought. Into video games since the 70's and still today. In my day, the cool thing was to have a train set. The bigger the setup, the more fun it was. TrainVR is the closest thing I've come across that allows me to revisit childhood. It IS Early Access, so it does come with a few issue's. More content and functionality should added to have this game fulfill itself. And the Devs are off to a great start! \nNow understand... I usually 'refund' as soon as I hit several problems. I prefer to pay when something is nearly polished. But as much as there are glitches in this game that can be frustrating at times, it IS SO MUCH FUN!  It is very useable and I've completed a few trainsets that ran without a glitch. But rIght now, for me, thats not the norm yet. Once you see the quality of what's gone into this, you know the Devs will fix things and hopefully add more content. Despite its early glitches, it does gives hours of fun. It's simplistic, graphics are excellent and it's super EZ to lose yourself for hours playing this. I will say that even though it needs some work, I still highly recommend it! It's only going to get better...",
